{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T20:24:28.296Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"**Findings**\n- Medium: [explain_export.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go:543) relies on `RewindPoint.SessionIDs` for multi-session filtering, but [explain.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:2169) never populates `SessionCount` or `SessionIDs` when building committed checkpoint points. The new JSON list also emits those fields, so multi-session checkpoints show only the latest session and `entire explain --json --session <older-session>` can miss valid checkpoints. Add an integration test using a real multi-session committed checkpoint through the JSON list path.\n\n- Medium: [explain_export.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go:528) fetches `limit+1`, truncates at [line 539](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go:539), then applies `--session` filtering at [line 545](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/explain_export.go:545). A session whose checkpoints are older than the first 100 branch checkpoints returns empty or incomplete JSON unless the caller guesses a larger `--limit`. Filter before applying the result cap, or make the cap explicitly a scan limit and test that behavior.\n\n- Low: [session_current.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/session_current.go:42) ignores the selected output mode when there is no active session. `entire session current --transcript > session.jsonl` exits 0 and writes `No active session found...` to stdout, corrupting the machine-readable stream. Add no-session tests for `--json` and `--transcript`, and return a mode-appropriate error or structured empty response.\n\n- Low: [recap.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/recap.go:157) never surfaces the new cancellation/timeout messages from [recap_errors.go](/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/recap_errors.go:15), because `shouldShowRecapLoadErrorMessage` only allows selected HTTP/network errors and `isRecapNetworkError` excludes context cancellation/deadline. The tests cover `recapLoadErrorMessage` directly, but not the actual handler path. Add handler tests for wrapped `context.Canceled` and `context.DeadlineExceeded`.\n\nReviewed committed changes only vs `origin/soph/add-codex-post-tool`; ignored unrelated dirty worktree changes. I did not run tests.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
